# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Installed character artwork. Whoever runs this instance holds the rights to
# whatever they put here, so nothing under it is committed — the folder ships
# with only its README and the one character below, and otherwise falls back to
# the built-in SVG mascots.
# `npm run fixtures:characters` writes placeholders here for testing.
/public/characters/*
!/public/characters/README.md

# Tally is the exception, and only Tally. It is not installed artwork — every
# vertex, material and animation clip in it is generated by
# `scripts/make-character-model.mjs`, which is in this repo, so the rights
# question the rule above exists to answer does not arise. Narrowed to this one
# path on purpose: the blanket rule still ignores every other folder here, and
# weakening it would quietly start committing whatever an owner dropped in.
!/public/characters/tally/
!/public/characters/tally/**
